# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SteamPipe leftovers
#
# The two folders below are why this section exists. Someone will eventually
# point Build output at a folder inside the repository, and a depot chunk cache
# is hundreds of megabytes of binary that must never reach a commit. Generated
# build scripts are ignored by default too — they are derived from a profile,
# not authored — but a project that wants its scripts under version control
# should un-ignore them deliberately rather than by accident.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
BuildOutput/
ContentBuilder/output/
*.csd
*.csm
depot_*_*.manifest
scripts/app_build_*.vdf
scripts/depot_build_*.vdf

# Never commit a steamcmd session: config.vdf holds a live refresh token that
# grants upload rights to the account.
config.vdf
ssfn*
steam_tokens.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Release archives
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Staging area for the files attached to a GitHub release. They are build output,
# roughly 42 MB per release, and GitHub stores release assets outside the git
# object database precisely so a clone does not have to carry every past build.
dist/
